-- title:
--   Riemann–Siegel sample data, segment 12, group 045, part 3 (heights ≈725093.6475–≈725230.4095)
-- statement:
--   Riemann–Siegel sample data for the zeros of $\zeta(1/2+it)$ with $t\in[≈725093.6475,\,≈725230.4095]$: part 3 of group 045 of segment 12 of the extension from height $100000$ to $10^6$.
--
--   Each band is a list of records of the structure `RS5.Sample` from the published framework: a dyadic height $t=tn/2^{16}$, a margin $E$ and integer hint fields for the Riemann–Siegel main sum. Consecutive bands share their endpoint sample.
--
--   The data were produced by a program and are not trusted; the kernel checks them in the problems named below. The problem `RH1E6S12.part_045_3` states that every band of the part passes the kernel-evaluated sharp band checker of the framework, which certifies a sign change of Hardy's $Z(t)$ between consecutive samples of opposite sign.
-- source:
